 Context

 This is the final domain from the original spec (Doc/Prompt/Prompt sections 7-9) and the one that ties every previous slice together: a Contractor is selected, a Work
 Order is issued against a specific Fund Allocation, milestone Payments are made against the work order, and an Inspection gates the final payment. It's also what
 finally uses Fund.spentAmount, which has sat at a hardcoded 0 since the Fund domain was built. And it closes out the last three unused ProjectStatus values (RUNNING,
 INSPECTION, COMPLETED) the same way Fund Allocation closed ALLOCATED.

 Source of truth

 Doc/Prompt/Prompt lines 241-302 (Work Order Management, Payment Management, Inspection).

 Key design decision: WorkOrder links to a specific FundAllocation, not just Project

 A Project can have more than one FundAllocation (funded across separate months). To know which Fund's spentAmount a Payment should draw down, WorkOrder needs a direct
 FK to the FundAllocation it's spending against — not just the Project. So WorkOrder carries both project and fundAllocation FKs (plus contractor), and Payment
 reaches the Fund via workOrder.fundAllocation.fund.

 New entities (package com.himaloyit.buildnation.cdm.*, table prefix cons_)

 WorkOrder — cons_work_order: id, workOrderNumber (unique, auto-generated WO-{year}-{seq}), project (FK), contractor (FK), fundAllocation (FK), amount, startDate,
 endDate (LocalDate), status (WorkOrderStatus: IN_PROGRESS, INSPECTION, COMPLETED, CANCELLED), createdAt/updatedAt.

 Payment — cons_payment: id, workOrder (FK), milestoneType (MilestoneType: ADVANCE, PROGRESS, FINAL — the spec's 30/40/30 split), percentage (Integer), amount
 (BigDecimal, computed = workOrder.amount * percentage / 100), status (PaymentStatus: REQUESTED, APPROVED, PAID, REJECTED), voucherNumber (nullable, auto-generated
 V-{year}-{seq} on PAID), requestedDate, approvedDate (nullable), paymentDate (nullable) — all LocalDate, createdAt/updatedAt.

 Inspection — cons_inspection: id, workOrder (FK), inspectorName, progressPercentage (Integer), quality (String), remarks (nullable String), status (InspectionStatus:
 PENDING, APPROVED, REJECTED), inspectionDate, createdAt/updatedAt. Photos deferred (same reasoning as Project — no MinIO/S3 yet).

 New exception: util/exceptions/InvalidStateException (400) — one shared exception for every business-rule/state-machine violation below (mirrors the existing
 EntityNotFoundException/InsufficientFundBalanceException handler pattern in GlobalResponseEntityException).

 Business rules and status cascades (this is the core of the domain)

 Creating a WorkOrder (WorkOrderService.createWorkOrder):
 - Validates project.status == ALLOCATED (else InvalidStateException) — a work order can't be issued before funds are allocated
 - Validates contractor.status != BLACKLISTED
 - Validates fundAllocation.project.id == project.id (the allocation must actually belong to this project) and request.amount <= fundAllocation.amount (can't contract
 for more than was allocated)
 - Generates workOrderNumber, sets status = IN_PROGRESS
 - Sets project.status = RUNNING via IProjectService.updateProjectStatus (same pattern FundAllocationService already uses)

 Creating an Inspection (InspectionService.createInspection):
 - Validates the work order isn't already COMPLETED/CANCELLED
 - Sets workOrder.status = INSPECTION (direct repo mutation, same pattern as Fund mutations in FundAllocationService) and project.status = INSPECTION via
 IProjectService

 Creating a Payment (PaymentService.createPayment):
 - Sums percentage across this work order's existing non-REJECTED payments; rejects if sum + new percentage > 100
 - Computes amount, sets status = REQUESTED, requestedDate = now

 Updating Payment status (PaymentService.updatePaymentStatus — one PATCH /{id}/status endpoint drives the whole state machine):
 - REQUESTED → APPROVED: if milestoneType == FINAL, requires an APPROVED Inspection to already exist for this work order (else InvalidStateException); sets
 approvedDate
 - APPROVED → PAID: generates voucherNumber, sets paymentDate; adds payment.amount to fund.spentAmount (via workOrder.fundAllocation.fund, direct IFundRepository
 mutation — first real consumer of that field); if milestoneType == FINAL, cascades workOrder.status = COMPLETED and project.status = COMPLETED via IProjectService
 - REQUESTED → REJECTED: allowed
 - Any other transition (e.g. REQUESTED → PAID directly, re-approving an already-PAID payment) → InvalidStateException

 Deleting a Payment: only allowed while status is REQUESTED or REJECTED — once APPROVED/PAID it's a financial record, not reversible through delete (else
 InvalidStateException).

 Pattern to follow (already established)

 - FK-validation + cross-service status cascade: FundAllocationService.createAllocation
 (constituency-development-management/src/main/java/com/himaloyit/buildnation/cdm/services/impl/FundAllocationService.java) — same shape for
 WorkOrderService/PaymentService: inject IProjectService for status changes, inject IFundRepository/IWorkOrderRepository directly for same-service-family field
 mutations
 - Sequential number generation: none exists yet — new pattern, small and self-contained (countByXStartingWith repository method + String.format)
 - Standard CRUD/status-PATCH shape: ProjectController/ContractorController for the rest of each controller (create/get/list/update/delete, by-<parent> filters)
 - Exception + handler: InsufficientFundBalanceException + its handler in GlobalResponseEntityException.java — copy this shape for InvalidStateException

 Standard file set per entity (WorkOrder, Payment, Inspection): domain/entities, domain/enums (WorkOrderStatus, MilestoneType, PaymentStatus, InspectionStatus),
 domain/dto, domain/mapper, domain/model (Create/Update requests + status-update requests), domain/repositories/iRepositories, services/iServices + services/impl,
 controllers/rest.

 Endpoints

 WorkOrderController (/api/v1/work-orders): create, get-by-id, paginated list, GET /by-project/{projectId}, GET /by-contractor/{contractorId}, update (amount/dates
 only), PATCH /{id}/status (manual override, e.g. to CANCELLED), delete.

 PaymentController (/api/v1/payments): create, get-by-id, paginated list, GET /by-work-order/{workOrderId}, PATCH /{id}/status (drives the state machine above), delete
 (with the REQUESTED/REJECTED-only guard).

 InspectionController (/api/v1/inspections): create, get-by-id, paginated list, GET /by-work-order/{workOrderId}, PATCH /{id}/status (approve/reject), update
 (remarks/quality/progress only), delete.

